---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Testimonials from "../../components/Testimonials.astro";
import NextProject from "../../components/NextProject.astro";

const jsonLd = [
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "CreativeWork",
    "name": "Crpton — Taking a clinic system off the desktop",
    "description": "Rebuilding a desktop-bound clinic system as a web app and companion mobile app — patient records, tooth charting, treatment plans and billing.",
    "url": "https://abdulazizabudhair.com/work/crpton",
    "image": "https://abdulazizabudhair.com/assets/img/og-crpton.jpg",
    "author": { "@type": "Person", "name": "Abdulaziz Abu Dhair", "url": "https://abdulazizabudhair.com/" },
    "creator": { "@type": "Person", "name": "Abdulaziz Abu Dhair", "url": "https://abdulazizabudhair.com/" },
    "genre": "Healthcare practice management",
    "inLanguage": "en"
  },
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
    "itemListElement": [
      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "https://abdulazizabudhair.com/" },
      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Work", "item": "https://abdulazizabudhair.com/#work" },
      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3, "name": "Crpton", "item": "https://abdulazizabudhair.com/work/crpton" }
    ]
  }
];
---
<Layout
  title="Crpton — Case Study · Abdulaziz Abu Dhair"
  description="Rebuilding a desktop-bound clinic system as a web app and companion mobile app — patient records, tooth charting, treatment plans and billing."
  path="/work/crpton"
  alternate="/ar/work/crpton"
  ogType="article"
  ogImage="og-crpton.jpg"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
<article class="case" aria-labelledby="case-title">
  <div class="container cs-hero">
    <a class="back-link text-link" href="/#work"><span aria-hidden="true">←</span> Back to portfolio</a>
    <p class="cs-hero__eyebrow">Case study · Healthcare · Practice Management</p>
    <h1 class="cs-hero__title" id="case-title">Crpton</h1>
    <p class="cs-hero__subtitle">Taking a clinic system off the desktop — desktop-bound clinic software, rebuilt as a browser-based web app and a companion mobile app, so doctors, and support, can reach it from anywhere.</p>
    <dl class="cs-hero__facts">
      <div><dt>My role</dt><dd>UX/UI Designer, solo end-to-end</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Platform</dt><dd>Web app + companion mobile app</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Timeline</dt><dd>9 months · May 2025 – Jan 2026</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Status</dt><dd class="cs-status"><span class="work-card__dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>Live in real clinics</dd></div>
    </dl>
    <nav class="cs-onthispage" aria-label="On this page">
      <span class="cs-onthispage__label">On this page</span>
      <a href="#overview">Overview</a>
      <a href="#decisions">Key decisions</a>
      <a href="#before-after">Before &amp; after</a>
      <a href="#mobile-app">Mobile app</a>
      <a href="#outcome">Outcome</a>
    </nav>
  </div>

  <div class="container">
    <div class="cs-panel" style={{ background: "var(--project-crpton)" }}>
      <img src="/assets/img/crpton-cs-hero-1040.webp" srcset="/assets/img/crpton-cs-hero-1040.webp 1040w, /assets/img/crpton-cs-hero-2080.webp 2080w" sizes="(min-width: 1280px) 1040px, 90vw" width="1040" height="659" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" alt="Crpton web app: a patient's finance tab showing total fees, payments, insurance and balance.">
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="container cs-section">
    <p class="fact-card__label">Project at a glance</p>
    <div class="cs-glance">
      <div class="fact-card">
        <p class="fact-card__value">2 platforms</p>
        <p class="fact-card__text">Browser-based web app + companion mobile app</p>
      </div>
      <div class="fact-card">
        <p class="fact-card__value">8 tabs</p>
        <p class="fact-card__text">Every patient record in one profile</p>
      </div>
      <div class="fact-card">
        <p class="fact-card__value">Live</p>
        <p class="fact-card__text">In daily use in real clinics — not a pilot</p>
      </div>
      <div class="fact-card">
        <p class="fact-card__value">2,000+</p>
        <p class="fact-card__text">Clinics &amp; clinicians across Palestine, Oman and Jordan</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="container cs-section" id="overview">
    <div class="cs-eyebrow"><span class="cs-eyebrow__square"></span>The challenge</div>
    <h2 class="cs-title">One machine, in one room.</h2>
    <div class="cs-prose">
      <div>
        <h3>Context</h3>
        <p>Crpton was clinic-management software installed on desktop computers in doctors’ clinics and medical centers — handling patients, treatment plans and billing. Being desktop-bound meant it lived on one machine, in one room.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Problem</h3>
        <p>When something broke, there was no easy fix. Support either had to send someone on-site or walk a doctor through a screen-share session mid-clinic — slow, disruptive, and dependent on the doctor being free. The software also couldn’t be reached from anywhere but that one desktop.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="container cs-section" id="decisions">
    <div class="cs-eyebrow"><span class="cs-eyebrow__square"></span>01 — Key decisions</div>
    <h2 class="cs-title">Six decisions that took <em>the clinic off the desktop</em></h2>
    <p class="cs-lead">Each one answers the same question: how does a doctor get to what they need, from wherever they are, without waiting on support?</p>
    <div class="cs-decisions">
      <div class="fact-card fact-card--decision"><p class="fact-card__label">01</p><p class="fact-card__value">Browser-based, not installed</p><p class="fact-card__text">A browser-based web app instead of installed software, so a doctor — or support — can open it from any device, without a site visit or screen-share.</p></div>
      <div class="fact-card fact-card--decision"><p class="fact-card__label">02</p><p class="fact-card__value">A companion mobile app</p><p class="fact-card__text">A condensed home (appointments, recalls, analytics) and a quick-access “Hub” menu, so a doctor can check on the clinic away from the desk.</p></div>
      <div class="fact-card fact-card--decision"><p class="fact-card__label">03</p><p class="fact-card__value">One patient, one profile</p><p class="fact-card__text">Every record in one profile with eight tabs — General, Dental, Finance, Medical, X-Ray, Prescription, Reports, Lab — so a doctor never loses the patient’s context.</p></div>
      <div class="fact-card fact-card--decision"><p class="fact-card__label">04</p><p class="fact-card__value">Billing inside the system</p><p class="fact-card__text">A per-patient finance view — fees, payments, insurance, balance — plus clinic-wide expense analytics, instead of a separate spreadsheet.</p></div>
      <div class="fact-card fact-card--decision"><p class="fact-card__label">05</p><p class="fact-card__value">Light, dark and larger text</p><p class="fact-card__text">Light/Dark/Auto themes and adjustable text size, since clinics run under different lighting and staff spend long shifts at the screen.</p></div>
      <div class="fact-card fact-card--decision"><p class="fact-card__label">06</p><p class="fact-card__value">An interactive tooth chart</p><p class="fact-card__text">Tap a tooth, tag the procedure, and it flows straight into a priced treatment plan — fast enough for chairside use.</p></div>
    </div>
    <figure style={{ marginTop: "48px" }}>
      <div class="cs-panel" style={{ background: "var(--project-crpton)" }}>
        <img src="/assets/img/crpton-cs-toothchart-1264.webp" srcset="/assets/img/crpton-cs-toothchart-1264.webp 1264w, /assets/img/crpton-cs-toothchart-2528.webp 2528w" sizes="(min-width: 1280px) 1264px, 90vw" width="1264" height="801" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Crpton's interactive tooth chart: tap a tooth, tag a procedure, add it to the treatment plan.">
      </div>
      <figcaption>The doctor selects a tooth and tags a procedure. The system adds it to a priced treatment plan.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>

  <div class="container cs-section" id="before-after">
    <div class="cs-eyebrow"><span class="cs-eyebrow__square"></span>02 — Before → after</div>
    <h2 class="cs-title">From one desktop <em>to any device</em></h2>
    <div class="cs-beforeafter">
      <div>
        <div class="cs-panel" style={{ background: "var(--muted)" }}>
          <img src="/assets/img/crpton-cs-before-600.webp" srcset="/assets/img/crpton-cs-before-600.webp 600w, /assets/img/crpton-cs-before-1200.webp 1200w" sizes="600px" width="600" height="286" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="The old desktop-only clinic software, installed on a single Windows machine.">
        </div>
        <p class="cs-ba-tag"><span>Before</span>Installed on one desktop, in one room</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="cs-panel" style={{ background: "var(--project-crpton)" }}>
          <img src="/assets/img/crpton-cs-after-600.webp" srcset="/assets/img/crpton-cs-after-600.webp 600w, /assets/img/crpton-cs-after-1200.webp 1200w" sizes="600px" width="600" height="380" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="The new Crpton web app, opened in a browser.">
        </div>
        <p class="cs-ba-tag cs-ba-tag--after"><span>After</span>A browser-based app any doctor can open from anywhere</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="container cs-section">
    <div class="cs-grid cs-grid--2">
      <figure>
        <div class="cs-panel" style={{ background: "var(--project-crpton)" }}>
          <img src="/assets/img/crpton-cs-platform-1-524.webp" srcset="/assets/img/crpton-cs-platform-1-524.webp 524w, /assets/img/crpton-cs-platform-1-1048.webp 1048w" sizes="524px" width="524" height="329" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Crpton patient profile with eight tabs: General, Dental, Finance, Medical, X-Ray, Prescription, Reports, Lab.">
        </div>
        <figcaption>One profile, eight tabs — the patient’s whole story without leaving the record.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure>
        <div class="cs-panel" style={{ background: "var(--project-crpton)" }}>
          <img src="/assets/img/crpton-cs-platform-2-524.webp" srcset="/assets/img/crpton-cs-platform-2-524.webp 524w, /assets/img/crpton-cs-platform-2-1048.webp 1048w" sizes="524px" width="524" height="332" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Crpton patient list with quick filters.">
        </div>
        <figcaption>Patient list with quick filters.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure>
        <div class="cs-panel" style={{ background: "var(--project-crpton)" }}>
          <img src="/assets/img/crpton-cs-platform-3-524.webp" srcset="/assets/img/crpton-cs-platform-3-524.webp 524w, /assets/img/crpton-cs-platform-3-1048.webp 1048w" sizes="524px" width="524" height="332" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Crpton clinic-wide expenses and transactions report.">
        </div>
        <figcaption>Clinic-wide expenses and transactions.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure>
        <div class="cs-panel" style={{ background: "var(--project-crpton)" }}>
          <img src="/assets/img/crpton-cs-platform-4-524.webp" srcset="/assets/img/crpton-cs-platform-4-524.webp 524w, /assets/img/crpton-cs-platform-4-1048.webp 1048w" sizes="524px" width="524" height="329" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Crpton reports with filters for the practice, in Arabic.">
        </div>
        <figcaption>Reports with filters for the practice.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="container cs-section" id="mobile-app">
    <div class="cs-eyebrow"><span class="cs-eyebrow__square"></span>03 — Companion app</div>
    <h2 class="cs-title">The clinic in <em>a doctor’s pocket</em></h2>
    <p class="cs-lead">Appointments, recalls and patient finances — in light and dark — for the moments between patients.</p>
    <div class="cs-grid cs-grid--4" style={{ "--project-tile": "var(--project-crpton)" }}>
      <figure><img src="/assets/img/crpton-cs-mobile-1-240.webp" srcset="/assets/img/crpton-cs-mobile-1-240.webp 240w, /assets/img/crpton-cs-mobile-1-480.webp 480w" sizes="240px" width="240" height="522" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Crpton mobile app home screen, light theme."><figcaption>Home · light</figcaption></figure>
      <figure><img src="/assets/img/crpton-cs-mobile-2-240.webp" srcset="/assets/img/crpton-cs-mobile-2-240.webp 240w, /assets/img/crpton-cs-mobile-2-480.webp 480w" sizes="240px" width="240" height="522" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Crpton mobile app home screen, dark theme."><figcaption>Home · dark</figcaption></figure>
      <figure><img src="/assets/img/crpton-cs-mobile-3-240.webp" srcset="/assets/img/crpton-cs-mobile-3-240.webp 240w, /assets/img/crpton-cs-mobile-3-480.webp 480w" sizes="240px" width="240" height="522" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Crpton mobile app patient profile screen."><figcaption>Patient profile</figcaption></figure>
      <figure><img src="/assets/img/crpton-cs-mobile-4-240.webp" srcset="/assets/img/crpton-cs-mobile-4-240.webp 240w, /assets/img/crpton-cs-mobile-4-480.webp 480w" sizes="240px" width="240" height="522" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Crpton mobile app finance screen."><figcaption>Finance</figcaption></figure>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="container cs-section">
    <figure class="cs-quote">
      <span class="cs-quote__mark" aria-hidden="true">&ldquo;</span>
      <blockquote><p>The Crpton dashboard reached a new level of quality thanks to Abdulaziz’s UX/UI expertise. His thoughtful design decisions greatly enhanced the overall user experience.</p></blockquote>
      <figcaption>
        <span class="testimonial-card__avatar" aria-hidden="true">AA</span>
        <span class="testimonial-card__who"><cite>Alaa Al-Najjar</cite><span>Founder, Crpton · Bethlehem, Palestine</span></span>
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>

  <div class="container cs-section" id="outcome">
    <div class="cs-eyebrow"><span class="cs-eyebrow__square"></span>04 — Outcome</div>
    <h2 class="cs-title">Live, and in daily use</h2>
    <div class="cs-outcome">
      <div>
        <h3>Outcome</h3>
        <p>Crpton is live and in daily use in real clinics today — not a pilot or a beta, but the system doctors and staff actually run their day on.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>What I learned</h3>
        <p>To design treatment plans, insurance flows and clinic billing that held up, I had to read into dentistry and accounting well enough to think like the people using the system every day. Learning the domain before trusting my own instincts is the lens I now bring to any specialized industry.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="container">
    <div class="cs-cta">
      <div>
        <h2>Running software stuck on one machine?</h2>
        <p>Tell me where your product is today, and how you’d like it to work.</p>
      </div>
      <a class="btn btn--primary btn--xl" href="/#contact">Let’s talk</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</article>

<NextProject current="crpton" />

<Testimonials />

</Layout>
